{
  "version": 1,
  "status": "review_pending",
  "note": [
    "Fallback adult reference ranges, used ONLY when a report does not print its",
    "own range (doc 21 §1.4). When the report prints one we compare against that,",
    "in the report's own units, and never touch this file — a lab's own range is",
    "the one its analyser was calibrated to.",
    "",
    "status=review_pending is load-bearing: until an oncologist signs this off,",
    "every flag derived from it is shown as a weaker, grey signal in the doctor's",
    "UI (ref_source='default'), not as an equal to a printed-range flag.",
    "",
    "Adults only. There are no paediatric ranges here and no pregnancy ranges;",
    "a test whose range genuinely depends on those is better left unflagged than",
    "flagged against the wrong population.",
    "",
    "'critical' thresholds change the ORDER values are shown in and nothing else.",
    "They are not an urgency decision and they never page anyone: red flags and",
    "escalation are deterministic clinical logic elsewhere (CODEBASE_MEMORY)."
  ],
